WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:06.220
Avengers: Endgame delivers an epic conclusion
for the MCU's founding fathers, Tony Stark

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.630
and Steve Rogers.

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:12.100
And that spectacular ending is one that Marvel
carefully constructed, laying an intricate

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.030
trail of clues over the past 22 movies.

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:19.770
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and today
I'm excited to reveal all the foreshadowing

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:24.350
and hidden symbolism in the MCU that cleverly
predicted Iron Man's ultimate destiny.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:28.359
Plus, I'll be breaking down every amazing
detail you might have missed in the Endgame

00:00:28.359 --> 00:00:32.140
finale and explaining what it means for the
future of the MCU.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:36.129
To celebrate the film's release, I'm kicking
off a special Marvel giveaway.

00:00:36.129 --> 00:00:38.660
Subscribe and leave a comment about the movie
for a chance to win.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:43.399
Obviously, we're in the Endgame now for spoilers,
so take care if you haven't seen the movie

00:00:43.399 --> 00:00:44.399
yet.

00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:47.270
As Tony himself says in this movie, 'part
of the journey is the end.'

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:52.130
And in the final big battle, after it seemed
like the Mad Titan would win yet again, Tony

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:56.899
made the ultimate sacrifice, stealing back
the Infinity Stones from Thanos and snapping

00:00:56.899 --> 00:00:58.519
them in his own gauntlet.

00:00:58.519 --> 00:01:02.899
This dusted Thanos and his army, but also
mortally wounded Tony as the radiation from

00:01:02.899 --> 00:01:05.530
the snap burned up his armour and body.

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:10.590
Tony's final words to the world before he
snapped were "I am Iron Man", a perfect retort

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:15.890
to Thanos's line 'I am inevitable' which the
Mad Titan uttered just before trying and failing

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:17.890
to snap for the last time.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:22.310
But more than that, Tony's final words are
also a perfect call-back to the end of the

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:24.960
first Iron Man movie which launched the MCU.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.340
"I'm just not the hero type.

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:28.340
Clearly.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:31.380
With this laundry list of character defects,
all the mistakes I've made.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:32.600
The truth is.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:34.680
I am Iron Man."

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:40.110
After what happened in Endgame, it's interesting
to look back to the Avengers early days together,

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:42.812
when Steve told Tony:
"The only thing you really fight for is yourself.

00:01:42.812 --> 00:01:47.310
You're not the guy to make the sacrifice play,
to lay down on a wire and let the other guy

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:48.310
crawl over you.

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:50.060
I think I would just cut the wire."

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:54.280
Yet Tony proved he was willing to sacrifice
himself for the greater good during the Battle

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:59.080
of New York and most recently in Endgame,
and even back when he faced off with Obadiah

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:00.080
Stane.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:04.500
But his ultimate sacrifice was most poignantly
foreshadowed in Age of Ultron when Tony talked

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:07.950
to Nick Fury about the terrible vision he'd
seen of his legacy.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:12.060
Scarlet Witch induced the vision in Tony,
but it was a product of his own fears about

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:16.870
the future and, as he explained to Fury, what
he dreaded most wasn't dying, but that he'd

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:18.790
watch the others die while he survived.

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:20.270
"And I'm the man who killed the Avengers.

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:21.820
I saw them all dead, Nick.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:22.820
I felt it.

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:24.120
The whole world, too.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.120
I was shown.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:28.470
Wasn't a nightmare, it was my legacy.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:29.990
The end of the path I started us on."

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:35.100
Some parts of Tony's vision such as the invading
Leviathans and Cap's broken shield did come

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.300
true during the final battle in Endgame.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:41.900
However, unlike Infinity War where Tony had
to watch many of his fellow heroes turn to

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:47.590
dust, this time he saved the Avengers and
died instead, creating the legacy he wanted.

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:52.220
Indeed, it's been clear since the very first
Iron Man movie just how crucial the notion

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:56.960
of legacy was to Tony, as even in those days
the idea of leaving behind a legacy of death

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:00.490
was something that weighed heavy on his mind:
"We're a weapons manufacturer.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:04.690
"Obie, I just don't want a body count to be
our only legacy."

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:09.959
Back then, Tony tried rewriting his legacy
by ending his company's manufacture of weapons;

00:03:09.959 --> 00:03:14.520
but that turned out to be small potatoes compared
to what he had to do to change his legacy

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:15.520
today.

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:18.740
"We can bust arms dealers all the livelong
day, but that up there, that's...

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:21.460
That's the endgame."

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:25.150
Doctor Strange knew that Iron Man was the
key to defeating Thanos.

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:31.349
In Infinity War, Strange checked over 14 million
scenarios and found only one where the Avengers

00:03:31.349 --> 00:03:32.920
triumphed over the Mad Titan.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:38.180
"I went forward in time to view alternate
futures.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:40.780
To see all the possible outcomes of the coming
conflict.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:43.540
How many did you see?

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:44.540
14,000,605.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:46.780
How many did we win?

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:47.780
One."

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:52.250
Once Doctor Strange knew this, he did a complete
180 on his previous threat that he'd sacrifice

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:57.190
Iron Man's life to save the Time Stone, and
instead he willingly gave the stone to Thanos

00:03:57.190 --> 00:04:00.450
in order to stop him from killing Tony.

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:02.060
"Stop.

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:05.780
Spare his life...
and I will give you the stone."

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:10.459
The Sorcerer Supreme knew Iron Man had to
survive through Infinity War and actually

00:04:10.459 --> 00:04:14.910
told Tony there was "no other way" just before
he faded to dust.

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:19.320
Then in Endgame, when Thanos was on the verge
of victory yet again after defeating each

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:24.820
of the heroes one-by-one, Doctor Strange reminded
Tony that he was the only person who could

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.370
win the battle for them.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:30.780
He did this by turning to Tony and holding
up a single finger, a reminder that Tony's

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:34.629
sacrifice was the one and only way to beat
Thanos.

00:04:34.629 --> 00:04:39.370
Looking back to Civil War then, when Hawkeye
called Tony 'the futurist' who 'sees all'

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:43.240
and 'knows what's best for you', whether you
like it or not, although that was an easter

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:48.340
egg to both the comics and Robert Downey Junior's
music album, and although Hawkeye was annoyed

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:53.600
and mocking Tony when he said it, it turns
out that Hawkeye's words were pretty accurate.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:58.029
Thanks to Doctor Strange, Tony was the only
living Avenger who realised there was just

00:04:58.029 --> 00:05:01.860
a single way to win the war they were waging
once and for all.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:05.699
As Thanos said in Infinity War, Tony was indeed
cursed with knowledge

00:05:05.699 --> 00:05:10.370
Tony's death is, of course, heart-breaking
as his friends and fellow Avengers Rhodey

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:15.439
and Peter Parker find him dying and Pepper
comes over and tells him he "can rest now".

00:05:15.439 --> 00:05:19.509
Even in Endgame, when Tony tried to stay away
from the Avengers and live a peaceful life

00:05:19.509 --> 00:05:22.569
with his daughter Morgan and Pepper, he couldn't
do it.

00:05:22.569 --> 00:05:26.589
When he solved the time travel conundrum that
the Avengers were facing, he felt he should

00:05:26.589 --> 00:05:30.969
lock the discovery away and destroy it so
he couldn't go off on another adventure.

00:05:30.969 --> 00:05:34.999
But the pull of the Iron Man suit and his
desire to be the hero and tech genius has

00:05:34.999 --> 00:05:39.499
always been too strong, from revealing himself
as Iron Man at the press conference in his

00:05:39.499 --> 00:05:44.039
first film to taking on his last, incredibly
dangerous mission in Endgame.

00:05:44.039 --> 00:05:49.240
For Tony, living and dying as Iron Man was
basically his destiny.

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:53.669
And what an amazing 11-year journey it's been
for his character and what a long way he's

00:05:53.669 --> 00:05:58.249
come from being a man reluctant to act against
terrorists using his company's weapons.

00:05:58.249 --> 00:06:00.180
"Are you going to do something about it?

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:01.249
Why should I do anything?

00:06:01.249 --> 00:06:02.960
They're going to kill me, you, either way.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:06.819
And if they don't, I'll probably be dead in
a week."

00:06:06.819 --> 00:06:10.370
To becoming a man prepared to offer himself
up for the good of others.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:15.509
Tony's final stand against Thanos was 'the
last act of defiance of the great Tony Stark',

00:06:15.509 --> 00:06:20.869
to quote Yinsen who urged Tony not to waste
his life just before he died saving the billionaire

00:06:20.869 --> 00:06:22.569
genius in Afghanistan.

00:06:22.569 --> 00:06:25.250
And Tony certainly took those words on board.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:30.930
Ultimately, then, what Tony told Pepper back
in 2008 about his evolution turned out to

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:34.050
be true:
"If I were Iron Man, I'd have this girlfriend

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:35.180
who knew my true identity.

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:40.210
She'd be a wreck, 'cause she'd always be worrying
that I was going to die, yet so proud of the

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:41.330
man I'd become.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:43.080
She'd be wildly conflicted."

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:47.659
Fortunately, as we see during Tony's voiceover
in Endgame, after his death his legacy has

00:06:47.659 --> 00:06:51.919
been to restore the heroes and people who
were snapped away, so he's brought a happy

00:06:51.919 --> 00:06:53.699
ending to many in the universe.

00:06:53.699 --> 00:06:58.810
And, for us in the audience, we can also feel
Tony's legacy during the memorial that Pepper

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:00.219
holds for him.

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:04.599
After she releases a wreath of flowers with
the "Proof that Tony Stark has a heart" arc

00:07:04.599 --> 00:07:09.219
reactor, the camera slowly pans over so many
of the wonderful characters we've been introduced

00:07:09.219 --> 00:07:14.449
to in the MCU, from the very first film through
to the penultimate movie, then finally on

00:07:14.449 --> 00:07:19.659
to Nick Fury, the man who laid the groundwork
to bring them all together in the MCU's very

00:07:19.659 --> 00:07:22.879
first post-credits scene in the Iron Man movie.

00:07:22.879 --> 00:07:27.330
What this scene really represents then is
the legacy of marvellous superheroes that

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:29.830
Iron Man has given to us, the fans.

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:33.960
By the way, there's a lovely little cameo
in this funeral scene by Harley Keener, the

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:36.870
young boy who Tony met in Iron Man 3.

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:42.249
It's the same actor, Ty Simpkins, and he's
standing behind Wanda, Bucky and Sam.

00:07:42.249 --> 00:07:45.460
Although these scenes have brought many to
tears, there's still another part to Tony's

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:49.949
legacy which is that his daughter Morgan looks
like she's inherited his desire to put on

00:07:49.949 --> 00:07:51.360
the Iron Man suit.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:55.509
She not only picks up an Iron Man helmet from
Tony's garage at the beginning of the movie,

00:07:55.509 --> 00:07:59.860
but just like her father, when Happy asks
Morgan what she'd like to eat, she asks for

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:03.870
a cheeseburger, which is exactly what Tony
demanded after he was brought back from Afghanistan.

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:04.949
"There are two things I want to do.

00:08:04.949 --> 00:08:09.699
I want an American cheeseburger, and the other...

00:08:09.699 --> 00:08:10.699
That's enough of that.

00:08:10.699 --> 00:08:11.699
Hogan, drive.

00:08:11.699 --> 00:08:12.699
Cheeseburger first."

00:08:12.699 --> 00:08:16.949
In Tony's BARF message, he also says that
Morgan will face the same forces of darkness

00:08:16.949 --> 00:08:21.909
and light that he battled during his life
and, in a tender moment, he echoes his daughter's

00:08:21.909 --> 00:08:26.089
words to him from earlier in the movie, "I
love you 3000."

00:08:26.089 --> 00:08:29.999
But there's one last tribute to the great
Tony Stark which you might just have missed

00:08:29.999 --> 00:08:33.180
unless you stayed right until the very end
of the credits.

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:37.729
Rather than an actual post-credits scene,
we just hear the sound of metal clanking over

00:08:37.729 --> 00:08:39.460
the Marvel Studios logo.

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:43.740
It's a call-back to the first Iron Man movie
when Tony had to forge his own Iron Man suit

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:45.350
while he was being held prisoner.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:50.221
And, of course, that cave scene was also referenced
at the beginning of Endgame when Tony and

00:08:50.221 --> 00:08:54.889
Nebula worked together to fix the ship's broken
fuel cells in a similar way to how Tony and

00:08:54.889 --> 00:08:57.920
Yinsen collaborated to make the suit in Iron
Man.

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:02.730
For me, Endgame's little post-credits teaser
symbolises not only that Iron Man was the

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:08.060
cornerstone of the MCU, his birth and death
bookending this chapter in the franchise's

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:13.580
history, but also how Tony's spirit and determination
lives on [in the Marvelverse], and how the

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:19.350
work he started still continues, with Marvel
busily putting together a new era of movies,

00:09:19.350 --> 00:09:22.520
TV shows, and stories for fans to enjoy.

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:26.880
Steve Rogers also got a big send-off in Endgame
and I've broken down everything you need to

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:31.589
know about the evolution of Captain America
in the MCU plus what Steve's ending with Peggy

00:09:31.589 --> 00:09:33.840
Carter really means in my next video.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:37.740
You can tap up right for the link to that
video or check the video description for the

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:39.290
link as soon as it's ready.

